 "rule": "For every order-book snapshot of a bucket with a tradeable book, take the newest scored decision of the same city-day at or before the snapshot (at most an hour before; tools/wxpredict/walkforward.py --dump, every probability out of sample). Buy one share of YES at the best ask when the probability is at least THETA above it, or one share of NO at its best ask (1 - best bid where the book gives no NO ask) when 1 - p is at least THETA above that. One share per bucket, side and day: the first snapshot that qualifies. Settled on the venue's winner. No fee. THETA 0.05 is the test; 0.02 and 0.10 are shown beside it. The same rule with the market's own normalised prices (q) is the control, which should not make money, and with the tempered market (q^a) the market's own calibration. The window is the event dates whose books are all in the repository: the archive's pruned books (data/archive/books) and the mirror's kept books (data/mirror/book_snapshots), which wait 16 days before they are mirrored.",
